# Unity CLI

The Unity Editor for this project must already be open before any `unity command` call. Run these from the repository root. If more than one Editor is open, pass `--project-path` with this repo's path.

The Pipeline server is localhost-only. It binds to `127.0.0.1` (ports 7800–7849) and refuses browser `Origin` requests. Leave the runtime server off. It is for development and QA players, disabled by default, and is not part of a release build. Do not aim `unity command --runtime` at a player you intend to ship.

`unity command eval` runs arbitrary C# on that local Editor. It is token-gated. Use it for a quick check that has no registered command. Prefer a registered command when one exists.

1. `unity pipeline list` — confirm this project shows Pipeline: Installed.
2. `unity command` — list the commands the connected Editor exposes, including the project commands below.
3. `unity command <name>` — run one command. Arguments use `--name value`.
4. `unity command eval "return Application.version;"` — a one-off read. `unity command eval_file` runs a `.cs` file the same way.

Project commands in `Assets/_Project/Editor/CliCommands`:

- `run_editmode_tests` — EditMode pass, fail, and skip counts plus leaf failures. The run is synchronous. Multi-frame `[UnityTest]` tests are excluded by Test Framework `runSynchronously`.
- `get_compile_and_console_errors` — `scriptCompilationFailed` plus compiler and console errors received after this domain loaded. Optional `--limit`. For the package's own console buffer, use the built-in `get_console_logs`.
- `list_project_avatars_and_clips` — `.vrm` and `.fbx` files and animation clips under `Assets/_Project`.
- `build_windows_player` — queues a Windows x64 development player at `Builds/Windows/BackseatCatgirl.exe` and returns immediately with status `queued`. That folder is gitignored. Poll `unity command build_status` until `status` is `completed` (`Succeeded` or `Failed` is on that report). The same queue is `unity command build --target StandaloneWindows64 --outputPath Builds/Windows/BackseatCatgirl.exe --options Development --confirm true`. Do not wait on `build_windows_player` for the player to finish; the CLI times out around 30 seconds and a player build takes longer. The command returns `error` when no scene is enabled, and `busy` when a build is already running.

After adding or editing a `[CliCommand]`, let the Editor finish recompiling, then run `unity command` again so the new name is listed. Built-in names such as `run_tests`, `build`, and `get_console_logs` belong to the package; the names above are this project's.
